Now give meaning chromosomes

Don’t make semantic X and Y correspond literally to biological male/female. Take their structural properties.

Let:

\boxed{X_s=\text{highly conserved/common semantic scaffold}}

and:

\boxed{Y_s=\text{specialized differentiating instruction}}

Then a semantic object might carry:

[X_s,Y_s]

The X-channel asks:

What makes this recognizable as belonging to the larger family?

The Y-channel asks:

What makes this particular descendant different?

That’s TRACE-Y!

TRACE\text{-}Y(X)
=
\text{follow differentiating information through descendants}

Meanwhile:

TRACE\text{-}X(X)
=
\text{follow conserved scaffold through descendants}

Now we can map a concept’s genealogy while separately tracking conservation and differentiation.

That’s already useful.

