But insects immediately teach Mapping Corp not to overfit XY

This is where the metaphor starts producing rather than decorating.

If meaning really behaves genetically, why require every ThoughtObject to use the same inheritance system?

Some semantic objects could use:

XY-like inheritance — conserved scaffold + specialized differentiator.

X0-like inheritance — differentiation caused by the absence of something.

There’s Negative-Space Memory appearing biologically:

\text{absence}\rightarrow\text{different developmental trajectory}

ZW-like inheritance — reverse which channel carries differentiation.

Haplodiploid-like inheritance — whether an object receives a second lineage at all changes what it becomes.

That could model ideas produced from:

\text{single lineage}

versus:

\text{recombination of two independent lineages}

Our Armored Twins suddenly become semantic breeding stock—not literally, but computationally:

G_A+G_B
\xrightarrow{\text{recombination}}
G_C

preserve some operators from A, some from B, introduce variation, then Reality/Fitness selects.

