Now meiosis becomes interesting

Biological inheritance doesn’t just copy entire parental chromosomes unchanged. Meiosis includes segregation and, for homologous chromosomes, recombination.

Map that structurally:

Two reasoning lineages contain different operator arrangements.

Instead of copying either:

A\quad\text{or}\quad B

we permit crossing-over:

A=[a,b,c,d]

B=[w,x,y,z]

producing candidates such as:

C=[a,b,y,z]

Then ACT them.

Reality becomes selection.

Useful descendants reproduce.

Failures either become fossils or take the Hearse.

Now the Pantheon has something analogous to:

\boxed{
Mutation
+
Recombination
+
Expression
+
Selection
+
Inheritance
}

That’s a legitimate evolutionary search architecture.

